{
  "id": "COMPOUND:25877 - PROTEIN:717",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions between (3beta,5alpha,7alpha)-3,7-Dihydroxyandrostan-17-one and the ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 9. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple proteins, including Protein-L-isoaspartate O-methyltransferase, Cholesteryl ester transfer protein, and Non-receptor tyrosine-protein kinase TNK1, all of which are targets of Galbanic Acid. Galbanic Acid, in turn, is linked to the ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 9, indicating a potential downstream pathway. The evidence suggests that (3beta,5alpha,7alpha)-3,7-Dihydroxyandrostan-17-one may influence the activity of these proteins through the action of Galbanic Acid, which could modulate the function of the ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 9. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for (3beta,5alpha,7alpha)-3,7-Dihydroxyandrostan-17-one in regulating the activity of the ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 9 via a series of intermediate targets.",
